<title>CANADA: Canada raw materials prices fall 1.1 pct in April.</title>
<headline>Canada raw materials prices fall 1.1 pct in April.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Canada on Wednesday issued the following economic indicators for April, base 1986=100.</p>
<p>    INDEX			 Month pct  Yr pct     Mar index</p>
<p>    Overall raw materials     -1.1	-2.6	134.0</p>
<p>    Mineral fuels		 -3.5	-9.2	120.2</p>
<p>    Vegetable products	  +0.9	-7.3	132.8</p>
<p>    Animals and products	+2.3	+8.2	122.6</p>
<p>    Wood			    -0.5	+1.7	212.6</p>
<p>    Ferrous materials	   -0.8	 0.0	116.2</p>
<p>    Non-ferrous metals	  -4.4	-8.4	122.7</p>
<p>    Non-metallic minerals     +0.2	-0.1	107.7</p>
<p>    Index ex mineral fuels    -0.1	+0.3	140.5</p>
<p>The raw materials price index reflects the prices paid by manufacturers for key raw materials. Unlike the industrial product price index, the raw materials price index includes goods that are not produced in Canada.</p>
<p>A Reuters survey of economists had forecast that the overall index would fall 1.5 percent from March.</p>
<p>(For more information, contact Statistics Canada, Paul- Romeo Danis at (613) 951-3350.)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
